		{"id":"00429451cc993dc4","type":"text","text":"Dialog:\n\n1. What do they keep steering the conversation towards?\n2. What are they avoiding?\n3. Interruptions\n4. Whad do they justify?","x":-63,"y":-592,"width":383,"height":312},
		{"id":"685d48282181f9b7","x":-146,"y":-220,"width":550,"height":1420,"type":"text","text":"📌 Save this BEFORE you write another chapter.\n\nAfter more than a decade working in publishing, I’ve learned that one of the biggest mistakes aspiring authors make happens long before they write page one.\n\nThey spend months, sometimes YEARS, writing a manuscript without first determining whether their idea is strong enough to succeed in the market.\n\nAnd here’s something most aspiring authors don’t realize: agents and publishers are evaluating far more than your ability to write beautiful prose.\n\nHere are 7 questions I want you to be able to answer:\n\n1. WHO is your ideal reader? Can you identify exactly who’s going to buy your book and what they’re already reading?\n\n2. WHAT is your book about? Can you communicate your central premise in one compelling sentence?\n\n3. WHAT makes it different? Why would someone choose your book over the other titles in its genre?\n\n4. WHAT are the stakes? What does your protagonist stand to lose, and why should readers care?\n\n5. WHERE does it belong? Do you understand your genre, market positioning, and comparable titles?\n\n6. DOES your story deliver? Does your plot build toward a satisfying ending that feels both surprising and inevitable?\n\n7. WHY are YOU writing it? What unique perspective, experience, or creative vision makes this story yours to tell?\n\nHere’s what I want every aspiring author to understand:\n\nBeautiful writing cannot compensate for a weak premise, unclear positioning, or a story that fails to deliver on its promise.\n\nAnd the sooner you identify those weaknesses, the easier they are to fix.\n\nThe strongest books begin with a strong foundation. And that foundation starts BEFORE page one.\n\nWant to know how strong YOUR book idea really is?"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}